# The ground control station (domains/teleoperation/console/) flying ArduPlane SITL on the sim's physics, as the
# operator sees it. Modelled on Mission Planner's planning docs (ardupilot.org/planner):
# where the console does something already, these say what it does; elsewhere they say what
# it should do. The console's driver (domains/teleoperation/console/src/expect.rs, `--station --expect`) clicks the real
# console; tests that need the mission file, the terrain check, the survey grid, measuring or
# the sim's window aren't supported yet.

Section: Ground control station
  The ground station flies the T1-S VTOL, the default plane of the sim, through [[ArduPilot]].
  (The plain T1-S Ranger has no flight controller, so it is flown from [[The simulator]].) You plan a
  [[mission]] on a map of the valley, and you write the mission to the plane. Then you arm
  the plane, and you throw it. The ground station talks to ArduPlane with [[MAVLink]], as
  Mission Planner and QGroundControl do.

  The console is one window with a set of screens. The [[tactical map]] (TACTICAL SITUATION)
  is in the middle. Its buttons are along the top: FOLLOW, GOTO, PLAN, ALT-, the plan
  altitude, ALT+, +TKOF, +RTL, CLEAR, UPLOAD, DOWNLOAD, EDIT and WP1. The vehicle command
  screen has ARM, DISARM and a button for each flight mode. Start with
  [[From plan to flight]].

Vocabulary:
  # The suite is about the desktop console, and the iOS app does the same job. Lines tagged
  # [iOS] are what differs there; see the expectation README, "Platforms" (https://github.com/ptescher/expectation).
  Platform: desktop | iOS
  State: the link is connected | lost
  State: the vehicle is disarmed | armed
    Shows: armed: the ARMED annunciator lights up
    Shows: disarmed: the ARMED annunciator goes out
  State: the autopilot mode is MANUAL | FBWA | FBWB | CRUISE | AUTO | RTL | LOITER | CIRCLE | GUIDED | TAKEOFF | QSTABILIZE | QHOVER | QLOITER | QLAND | QRTL
    Set: press {value} on the vehicle command screen
    Shows: the {value} button lights up
    Shows: stays the same: the mode does not change, and the AUTO button shows AUTO: NO MISSION?
  State: the map tool is pan | PLAN | GOTO
    Shows: pan: the map is back to panning
    Shows: PLAN: the PLAN button lights up
    Shows: GOTO: the GOTO button lights up
  State: the plan has 0..650 items
    Shows: the UPLOAD button reads UPLOAD {value}
    Shows: goes up by 1: a new marker appears at the end of the dashed plan, and the count on UPLOAD goes up by 1
    Shows: goes down by 1: the last marker goes away from the dashed plan, and the count on UPLOAD goes down by 1
    Shows: stays the same: the dashed plan and the count on UPLOAD do not change
  State: the plan altitude is 10..300 m
    Set: set the plan altitude to {value} with ALT- and ALT+
    Shows: the plan altitude between ALT- and ALT+ reads {value} m
    Shows: goes up by 10 m: the plan altitude between ALT- and ALT+ goes up by 10 m
    Shows: goes down by 10 m: the plan altitude between ALT- and ALT+ goes down by 10 m
    Shows: stays the same: the plan altitude between ALT- and ALT+ does not change
  State: the last plan item is none | TAKEOFF | WAYPOINT | LOITER_UNLIM | LOITER_TURNS | LAND | RTL
    Set: change the last item's command to {value}
    Shows: the last item of the dashed plan is {value}
  State: the takeoff is planned | not planned
    Shows: planned: the first item of the plan is a takeoff at home
    Shows: not planned: the plan has no takeoff
  State: the newest waypoint is at the plan altitude | at another altitude
    Shows: at the plan altitude: the new waypoint goes at the altitude between ALT- and ALT+
    Shows: at another altitude: the waypoints that are already in the plan keep their altitude
  State: the vehicle mission is empty | up to date | out of date
    Shows: up to date: the solid line of the mission on the vehicle is the same as the dashed plan
    Shows: out of date: the dashed plan and the solid line of the mission on the vehicle are different
    Shows: stays the same: the solid line of the mission on the vehicle does not change
  State: the home position is set | not set
    Shows: set: the map marks home where the plane was armed
    Shows[iOS]: set: the HOME badge turns green
  State: the waypoints are unchecked | clear of the terrain | too low somewhere
    Shows: clear of the terrain: each waypoint is above the ground below it
  State: the mission file is missing | up to date | out of date
    Shows: up to date: the file has the plan as it is now
    Shows: out of date: the plan is different from the file
  State: the measured distance is hidden | shown
    Shows: shown: the distance between the two points is shown on the map
  State: the vehicle's current item is 0..650
    Shows: item {value} is the current item, which is magenta on the map
    Shows: goes up by 1: the next item becomes the current item, which is magenta on the map
    Shows: stays the same: the current item does not change

  Event: the operator toggles the planning tool
    Say: press PLAN
  Event: the operator toggles the fly-to tool
    Say: press GOTO
  Event: the operator clicks the map
    Say: click the map
  Event: the operator right-clicks the map
    Say: right-click the map
  Event: the operator raises the plan altitude
    Say: press ALT+
  Event: the operator lowers the plan altitude
    Say: press ALT-
  Event: the operator adds a takeoff
    Say: press +TKOF
  Event: the operator adds a return home
    Say: press +RTL
  Event: the operator clears the plan
    Say: press CLEAR
  Event: the operator uploads the plan
    Say: press UPLOAD
  Event: the operator downloads the vehicle's mission
    Say: press DOWNLOAD
  Event: the operator edits the vehicle's mission
    Say: press EDIT
  Event: the operator restarts the mission
    Say: press WP1
  Event: the operator arms the vehicle
    Say: press ARM. Then press CONFIRM ARM in three seconds or less
    Say[iOS]: tap ARM. Then tap CONFIRM ARM in three seconds or less
  Event: the operator disarms the vehicle
    Say: press DISARM
    Say[iOS]: tap DISARM
  Event: the operator switches to AUTO
    Say: press AUTO
  Event: the operator switches to AUTO anyway
    Say: press AUTO. The button shows AUTO: NO MISSION? for four seconds. In that time, press it again
  Event: the operator saves the plan to a file
  Event: the operator loads the plan from the file
  Event: the operator checks the heights against the terrain
  Event: the operator draws a survey grid
  Event: the operator measures between two points
  Event: the pilot throws the plane in the sim
    Say: click the sim window. Then press Space to throw the plane
  Event: the plane reaches a waypoint
  Event: the plane reaches the last item

  Phrase: the console is connected to a plane on the ground
    Say: install Rust and Docker Desktop. Then run `cd domains/teleoperation/console && cargo run --release -- --station`. The first time, it builds ArduPlane [[SITL]], which takes approximately 15 minutes. After that, it starts in a few seconds. Three windows open: the console, the [[sensor feed]] and the sim. The console connects to the plane. The plane is on the ground and disarmed, in MANUAL, with home set and no plan. Wait until the ARM button shows ARM, not ARM: NOT READY
    Given the link is connected
    And the game clock is off
    And the vehicle is disarmed
    And the autopilot mode is MANUAL
    And the map tool is pan
    And the plan has 0 items
    And the plan altitude is 40 m
    And the last plan item is none
    And the takeoff is not planned
    And the vehicle mission is empty
    And the home position is set
    And the waypoints are unchecked
    And the mission file is missing
    And the measured distance is hidden
    And the plane is on the ground
    And the vehicle's current item is 0

  Phrase[iOS]: the console is connected to a plane on the ground
    Say: install the app on an iPhone or in the Simulator, and start ArduPlane [[SITL]] on your Mac (`ardupilot/run_sitl.sh`). Open the app. It connects to the plane on `tcp:5760`. The plane is on the ground and disarmed, in MANUAL, with home set. Wait until the ARM button shows ARM
    Given the link is connected
    And the vehicle is disarmed
    And the autopilot mode is MANUAL
    And the home position is set

  Phrase: the operator plans two waypoints
    Say: click the map at two points over the valley floor near home
    When the operator clicks the map
    When the operator clicks the map

  Phrase: the operator plans three waypoints
    Say: click the map at three points over the valley floor near home
    When the operator clicks the map
    When the operator clicks the map
    When the operator clicks the map


  # A radio (see Flying with a radio)
  State: the radio is calibrated | not calibrated
    Shows: calibrated: the sim says Radio calibrated and saved to controls.cfg, and the sticks and switches of the radio work
    Shows: not calibrated: the sim has not seen this radio's sticks, and its switches do nothing
  Event: the pilot calibrates the radio
    Say: press F2 in the sim window, and follow the prompts on the screen. Do each step in order: put the sticks in the middle with the throttle all the way down, and press Enter. Push the aileron stick right, the elevator stick up and the rudder stick right, one at a time, and hold each one until the prompt changes. Push the throttle stick all the way up. Then the sim asks for buttons for its other functions, one at a time: press Enter to skip all of them, because the arm switch, the mode buttons and the camera knobs are channels, and [[Setting up the TX15]] shows how the sim reads them
  State: the throttle stick is low | middle | high
    Set: move the throttle stick to the {value} position: all the way down is low, the middle is middle, and three quarters up is high
    Shows: low: the third number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1000
    Shows: middle: the third number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1500
    Shows: high: the third number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1750
  State: the arm switch is off | on
    Set: put the arm switch {value}: SE pressed in is on, and SE out is off (with a toggle fitted in place of the button, up is on and down is off)
    Shows: on: the first number after the slash in the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1900
    Shows: off: the first number after the slash in the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1100
  State: the mode switch is QHOVER | QLOITER | FBWA | CRUISE | AUTO | QRTL
    Set: press the button for {value} on the front of the radio: button 1 is QHOVER, 2 is QLOITER, 3 is FBWA, 4 is CRUISE, 5 is AUTO and 6 is QRTL
    Shows: the second number after the slash in the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is the one for {value}

  State: the aileron stick is left | centred | right
    Set: move the aileron stick {value}: all the way left, in the middle, or all the way right
    Shows: left: the first number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1250
    Shows: centred: the first number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1500
    Shows: right: the first number of the RC 1-4 line on the SYSTEMS screen is near 1750
  State: the VTOL's wings are level | banked
    Shows: level: the horizon in the PFD is flat, and the roll reading is near 0
    Shows: banked: the horizon in the PFD is tilted, and the roll reading is more than 10° from 0
  State: the last landing is soft | hard
    Shows: soft: the plane touches the ground at less than 2 m/s, and the HUD of the sim does not say CRASHED
    Shows: hard: the plane touches the ground at 2 m/s or more

  Event: the pilot switches to forward flight
    Say: push the throttle stick all the way up, pull the elevator stick back a little, and press button 3 on the front of the radio. The wing motors tilt forward and the plane speeds up
  Event: the pilot switches back to a hover
    Say: centre the elevator stick, put the throttle stick in the middle, and press button 2 on the front of the radio. The plane slows down and the wing motors tilt up

  Event: the pilot switches to QHOVER
    Say: press button 1 on the front of the radio. The plane stays in the air, and the wind can move it
  Event: the pilot switches to cruise
    Say: press button 4 on the front of the radio, with the throttle stick up. The wing motors tilt forward and the plane flies on its wing
  Event: the pilot sends the plane home
    Say: press button 6 on the front of the radio. The plane flies to home, and lands there

  State: the radio line is USB | serial
    Shows: USB: the sim reads the TX15 as a USB game controller (HID)
    Shows: serial: the station was started with --flight-computer, and the sim reads the TX15 from the flight computer's serial line

  Phrase: the TX15 is ready
    Say: connect the TX15 to the flight computer's serial line (start the station with --flight-computer, or give the radio a serial device with --tx15-serial). Set the radio up once, as [[Setting up the TX15]] shows: load the model with the six buttons on channel 8. Then put the throttle stick all the way down, SE out and press button 1
    Given the radio line is serial
    And the throttle stick is low
    And the arm switch is off
    And the mode switch is QHOVER
    And the TX15 screen arming is disarmed

  # A VTOL (see Flying a VTOL)
  State: the airframe is conventional | VTOL
  State: the flight is grounded | hovering | in transition | cruising
    Shows: grounded: the plane is on the ground, and the speed in the PFD is 0
    Shows: hovering: the plane stays at one place in the air, and the speed in the PFD is near 0
    Shows: in transition: the speed in the PFD goes up or down between 0 and the cruise speed
    Shows: cruising: the speed in the PFD is above 11 m/s, and the plane flies forward
  State: the height above home is 0..300 m
    Shows: the ALT REL line on the SYSTEMS screen reads {value} m
  State: the battery current is 0..100 A
    Shows: the BATTERY line on the SYSTEMS screen reads {value} A
  State: the battery voltage is 0..30 V
    Shows: the BATTERY line on the SYSTEMS screen reads {value} V
  Event: the operator takes off vertically
    Say: press VTOL TKOF. The plane climbs straight up to the plan altitude
  Event: the operator switches to forward flight
    Say: press CRUISE. The wing motors tilt forward and the plane speeds up
    Say[iOS]: tap CRUISE. The wing motors tilt forward and the plane speeds up
  Event: the operator switches to hover
    Say: press QLOITER. The plane slows down and the wing motors tilt up
    Say[iOS]: tap QLOITER. The plane slows down and the wing motors tilt up
  Event: the operator lands vertically
    Say: press QLAND. The plane comes down straight and stops its motors
    Say[iOS]: tap QLAND. The plane comes down straight and stops its motors

  Phrase: the console is connected to a VTOL on the ground
    Say: the station flies the T1-S VTOL, the default plane, with its two tilt-rotors and its rear rotor. The console shows the Q modes (QHOVER, QLOITER, QLAND and QRTL) with the other modes. Wait until the ARM button shows ARM, not ARM: NOT READY
    Given the console is connected to a plane on the ground
    And the airframe is VTOL

  Phrase: the VTOL is hovering
    Say: arm the plane, and press VTOL TKOF. Wait until the plane has climbed to the plan altitude and stopped
    Given the vehicle is armed
    And the flight is hovering
    And the height above home is at least 15 m

Background:
  Given the console is connected to a plane on the ground
